WEBVTT

00:00:01.060 --> 00:00:03.360
In order to save Pantasia from a danger to its very existence,

00:00:03.360 --> 00:00:06.150
Kazuma and the gang aim to win the Monaco Cup.

00:00:06.570 --> 00:00:07.070
And...

00:00:07.070 --> 00:00:09.070
unbeknownst to everyone else,

00:00:09.070 --> 00:00:11.360
Kanmuri granted Kawachi the means to that end.

00:00:12.160 --> 00:00:13.120
You are Rodin.

00:00:13.120 --> 00:00:15.080
Become the Ten Billion Yen Rodin.

00:00:15.080 --> 00:00:17.200
A-A Ten Billion Yen Rodin?!

00:00:25.050 --> 00:00:27.050
What have I...?

00:00:27.050 --> 00:00:29.750
Then, let’s have you show us, Kawachi, shall we?

00:00:30.380 --> 00:00:31.470
All right.

00:00:31.470 --> 00:00:32.260
I’m a man as well.

00:00:32.890 --> 00:00:33.930
I’ll show you.

00:00:33.930 --> 00:00:36.260
The Kawachi style of taking responsibility.

00:00:37.270 --> 00:00:41.350
I will be the host for this event.

00:00:41.350 --> 00:00:43.770
My name is Pierrot Bolneze.

00:00:46.480 --> 00:00:49.780
Isn’t this bread a little too big?

00:00:49.780 --> 00:00:54.030
I-I wasn’t expecting it to be so hard to breathe, and...

00:00:54.950 --> 00:00:58.080
When I had the flour put on me while I was naked...

00:00:58.080 --> 00:01:00.040
I seem to have chilled my stomach.

00:01:00.870 --> 00:01:01.870
All right.

00:01:03.120 --> 00:01:05.000
It’s cold!

00:01:05.460 --> 00:01:08.250
But, the plan was a mission from hell,

00:01:08.260 --> 00:01:11.880
one that would call forth a terrible
consequence with even one misstep.

00:01:11.880 --> 00:01:15.300
I can’t take this anymore!

00:01:23.480 --> 00:01:24.440
Princess!

00:01:26.020 --> 00:01:28.480
I-It’s a nightmare...

00:01:29.530 --> 00:01:31.740
Move!

00:01:31.740 --> 00:01:33.450
I can’t hold it in anymore!

00:01:36.490 --> 00:01:38.160
They’re really depressed.

00:01:38.870 --> 00:01:40.740
While it may have only been
an exhibition...

00:01:40.750 --> 00:01:44.160
On top of seriously insulting this tournament, Japan has

00:01:44.170 --> 00:01:47.500
assaulted Princess Anne,
from the Kingdom of Panquita.

00:01:48.420 --> 00:01:51.670
We’ve received a severe warning from
the Management Board of the Monaco Cup.

00:01:52.300 --> 00:01:54.590
We’ve also lost 2 points.

00:01:56.140 --> 00:01:59.100
This is a match with 10 points in total,

00:01:59.850 --> 00:02:02.680
so from the very beginning we have
no choice but to fight with only 8 points.

00:02:04.230 --> 00:02:06.940
We weren’t even late, and yet we lost points...

00:02:06.940 --> 00:02:08.230
It’s really cruel.

00:02:11.110 --> 00:02:13.360
There’s English bread, German bread, and French bread,

00:02:13.360 --> 00:02:15.280
but Japan’s bread, <i>Japan</i>, does not exist.

00:02:15.280 --> 00:02:17.570
In that case, there’s no choice but to create it.

00:02:17.570 --> 00:02:20.970
This story is a serious, biographical ballad of a boy who possesses Solar Hands,

00:02:20.970 --> 00:02:26.210
Azuma Kazuma, who will create a Japanese bread made by and for the Japanese people,

00:02:26.210 --> 00:02:29.540
which can be presented to the world proudly.

00:04:01.220 --> 00:04:01.860
The roulette that brings forth a storm!
This is the world level!!

00:04:01.860 --> 00:04:03.860
This is the world level!!

00:04:03.860 --> 00:04:06.980
The roulette that brings forth a storm!

00:04:15.820 --> 00:04:19.610
And now, we will begin the Second Monaco Cup.

00:04:19.610 --> 00:04:22.280
To begin with, we have the parade
of the participating countries.

00:04:23.830 --> 00:04:26.450
First, we have last year’s championship team.

00:04:27.950 --> 00:04:31.340
Our country France’s representatives, Kayser.

00:04:34.390 --> 00:04:36.210
Good luck, Kayser!

00:04:36.210 --> 00:04:37.670
We’re leaving it to you, Kayser!

00:04:37.670 --> 00:04:40.010
Just as you would expect of the championship seeds.

00:04:40.010 --> 00:04:42.300
Their odds of winning are an impressive 1.5 to 1,

00:04:42.300 --> 00:04:44.180
and of course,
they have the most popularity!

00:04:44.180 --> 00:04:45.550
Ein!

00:04:45.550 --> 00:04:46.930
Zwei!

00:04:46.930 --> 00:04:48.640
Drei!

00:04:48.640 --> 00:04:52.440
Also! Next, we have the entry of
the howling German representatives.

00:04:52.440 --> 00:04:57.440
And, as we’d expect, we have the Great
Britain representatives on their bagpipes.

00:04:59.540 --> 00:05:01.450
It sounds like they’re really having fun out there.

00:05:01.450 --> 00:05:02.780
Just as you’d expect
of a world competition.

00:05:02.780 --> 00:05:03.950
It’s quite a party.

00:05:05.170 --> 00:05:07.450
And contrary to that, we are...

00:05:07.870 --> 00:05:10.620
Hey, everyone, we’re going to be called out soon...

00:05:10.620 --> 00:05:13.170
Let’s do this with energy.

00:05:13.170 --> 00:05:14.960
Losing 2 points isn’t a big deal!

00:05:15.480 --> 00:05:16.850
That’s true.

00:05:17.350 --> 00:05:18.960
Slash your stomach.

00:05:19.300 --> 00:05:23.050
Who do you think is the
cause of these unpleasant feelings?

00:05:23.970 --> 00:05:27.800
And at number 78, we have
the Japanese representatives!

00:05:29.150 --> 00:05:30.140
Let’s go!

00:05:30.140 --> 00:05:31.060
All right!

00:05:34.060 --> 00:05:36.150
Go back home, you shameless people!

00:05:36.150 --> 00:05:36.950
You crap-in-your-underwear man!

00:05:36.950 --> 00:05:37.730
You changed your underwear, right?

00:05:37.730 --> 00:05:39.070
Someone like you shouldn’t be making bread!

00:05:39.070 --> 00:05:41.990
Oh, things are getting heated up here.

00:05:41.990 --> 00:05:44.570
Last year, the Japanese
representatives failed in the preliminaries.

00:05:44.570 --> 00:05:48.570
To top that off, this year, the Japanese representatives messed up <i>BIG</i> in the exhibition.

00:05:48.570 --> 00:05:51.620
They have to start the
preliminaries with a two point deduction.

00:05:51.620 --> 00:05:56.130
They have the lowest odds of over 300 to 1,
as well as the worst reputation this tournament.

00:05:56.130 --> 00:05:58.210
I guess that not a single person is betting on them.

00:05:58.210 --> 00:06:00.300
Wa, ha, ha, and ha.

00:06:01.350 --> 00:06:02.720
It’s all right.

00:06:02.720 --> 00:06:04.300
It’s all right this way.

00:06:04.300 --> 00:06:07.300
We can just pretend that
the jeers are cheers!

00:06:10.340 --> 00:06:12.350
Ouch...

00:06:13.400 --> 00:06:15.350
What the hell are you doing?!

00:06:15.350 --> 00:06:18.690
How exactly is it that you
manage to hear these jeers as cheers?!

00:06:18.690 --> 00:06:19.860
Calm down.

00:06:19.860 --> 00:06:22.360
Anything, and everything, is your fault!

00:06:22.360 --> 00:06:25.780
How much longer are you
going to harp on about the past,

00:06:25.780 --> 00:06:27.110
you ugly, old samurai!

00:06:27.110 --> 00:06:29.700
You should just die and
atone for your sins!

00:06:29.700 --> 00:06:31.700
I don’t want to die!

00:06:32.910 --> 00:06:33.380
Hey, hey!

00:06:33.380 --> 00:06:35.120
Why don’t you just cut your stomach?!
Hey, hey!

00:06:35.120 --> 00:06:35.910
Shut up, Baldy!

00:06:35.910 --> 00:06:38.040
Ooh la la!

00:06:38.040 --> 00:06:40.780
It looks like there is a falling out among friends.

00:06:40.780 --> 00:06:43.210
What is Japan thinking of?

00:06:43.210 --> 00:06:44.170
Ha, ha, and ha!

00:06:45.890 --> 00:06:47.380
This is the pits...

00:06:49.230 --> 00:06:50.470
Brother,

00:06:50.470 --> 00:06:54.390
I guess we don’t have to worry
about people like that after all, right?

00:06:54.390 --> 00:06:57.860
Edward, do not let your guard down.

00:06:57.860 --> 00:07:00.770
We must remember that
they are Kirisaki’s subordinates.

00:07:00.770 --> 00:07:04.400
I can’t imagine that he would send
useless people two years in a row.

00:07:04.890 --> 00:07:07.700
Especially that boy with the hairband.

00:07:07.700 --> 00:07:11.820
He possessed a La Main De Deesse
that surpassed even ours.

00:07:11.820 --> 00:07:16.330
This comes only to those who have trained
the flexibility of their hands since childhood.

00:07:16.330 --> 00:07:20.420
The suppleness of the joints of
these feminine hands and fingers

00:07:20.420 --> 00:07:23.890
is what produces soft and artistic bread.

00:07:24.220 --> 00:07:25.800
This Japanese representative...

00:07:25.800 --> 00:07:27.170
Has the Goddess’s Hands?!

00:07:27.170 --> 00:07:29.180
Anyone can do this!

00:07:30.440 --> 00:07:31.890
What is he?!

00:07:32.270 --> 00:07:33.890
Is he human?

00:07:37.360 --> 00:07:40.100
It would be safe to think of
him as a considerable opponent.

00:07:40.100 --> 00:07:41.350
I see.

00:07:43.870 --> 00:07:44.580
All right.

00:07:44.580 --> 00:07:47.950
Since there are 135
countries gathered here to participate,

00:07:47.950 --> 00:07:49.860
let me explain the rules
for the preliminaries.

00:07:50.670 --> 00:07:52.530
The preliminaries are based on a scoring system.

00:07:52.530 --> 00:07:54.790
In the first preliminaries, 5 points is
considered to be a perfect score.

00:07:54.790 --> 00:07:57.330
In the second preliminaries, 5 points is
also considered to be a perfect score.

00:07:57.330 --> 00:07:59.870
The points from the first and
second preliminaries will be added up,

00:07:59.870 --> 00:08:02.040
and 16 countries with the highest scores

00:08:02.040 --> 00:08:06.510
will be permitted entry into the Finals Leagues.

00:08:06.510 --> 00:08:07.880
In other words,

00:08:07.880 --> 00:08:10.630
since we have already lost 2 points,

00:08:10.630 --> 00:08:13.350
even if we pass the first and
second preliminaries with full points,

00:08:13.350 --> 00:08:15.470
we won’t have more than 8 points.

00:08:15.470 --> 00:08:16.800
It’s your fault.

00:08:30.790 --> 00:08:33.200
Wow, it’s a huge roulette wheel!

00:08:33.200 --> 00:08:37.240
This is the Grand Casino’s special “ingredient roulette.”

00:08:37.240 --> 00:08:40.670
In addition to numbers in the slots, we have ingredients!

00:08:40.670 --> 00:08:42.910
That’s a roulette wheel you don’t see every day...

00:08:42.910 --> 00:08:44.960
In the first preliminaries,

00:08:44.960 --> 00:08:48.170
you may use any variety of
flour, or any strain of yeast.

00:08:48.170 --> 00:08:49.920
Also, aside from sea water,
you may use any type of water.

00:08:49.920 --> 00:08:50.800
However...

00:08:50.800 --> 00:08:53.340
As for other ingredients, if you do
not get them from the roulette wheel,

00:08:53.340 --> 00:08:56.680
you may not use even things such as salt or sugar.

00:08:56.680 --> 00:08:58.180
W-What was that?!

00:08:58.180 --> 00:09:00.560
Each of the three members
from each nation’s representatives

00:09:00.560 --> 00:09:02.270
will spin the roulette ball, one by one,

00:09:02.270 --> 00:09:05.190
and using only the three ingredients that you land on,

00:09:05.190 --> 00:09:08.690
you must bake your bread!

00:09:11.000 --> 00:09:12.190
I’m worried.

00:09:12.640 --> 00:09:16.580
Yeah, this preliminary depends quite a bit on your luck.

00:09:16.580 --> 00:09:19.700
At the very least, we’d like to get salt or sugar...

00:09:20.510 --> 00:09:23.870
But, last year, there was a team that didn’t get either,

00:09:23.870 --> 00:09:26.960
and tried to draw salt from their sweat...

00:09:26.960 --> 00:09:28.300
in the open-air lobby.

00:09:34.900 --> 00:09:36.640
I can’t dance anymore.

00:09:36.640 --> 00:09:38.310
Just... Just a little more.

00:09:38.310 --> 00:09:38.980
Hang in there!

00:09:45.950 --> 00:09:48.020
Oh yeah, there was something like that...

00:09:48.020 --> 00:09:49.860
Oh well...

00:09:49.860 --> 00:09:52.320
While that’s a possibility,

00:09:52.320 --> 00:09:54.030
about half of the hundred slots are either salt or sugar.

00:09:54.560 --> 00:09:56.620
If you don’t try missing it on purpose,

00:09:56.620 --> 00:09:58.620
you might end up with all three landing on salt,

00:09:58.620 --> 00:10:01.280
so that in the end, you can only use salt.

00:10:01.280 --> 00:10:03.710
It’s hard, isn’t it?

00:10:03.710 --> 00:10:05.080
We have no choice but to pray

00:10:05.080 --> 00:10:07.750
that none of them fall on the
same spot, so that they can

00:10:07.750 --> 00:10:08.840
use as many ingredients as possible.

00:10:08.840 --> 00:10:09.500
Yeah...

00:10:09.760 --> 00:10:11.670
All right, then.

00:10:11.670 --> 00:10:14.220
Let us determine what
ingredients you can use by the roulette!

00:10:14.220 --> 00:10:15.510
Begin!

00:10:21.100 --> 00:10:22.270
All right.

00:10:22.270 --> 00:10:23.600
I’ll go first.

00:10:33.700 --> 00:10:34.690
It’s gonna drop.

00:10:43.460 --> 00:10:45.080
It’s eggs!

00:10:45.080 --> 00:10:46.210
We got eggs!

00:10:47.630 --> 00:10:51.050
There’s only two spots for eggs in the hundred.

00:10:51.050 --> 00:10:52.250
It’s amazing for him to get it.

00:10:52.250 --> 00:10:54.210
Yeah. Kazuma’s in luck.

00:10:54.210 --> 00:10:57.130
All right, I’ll go next.

00:10:57.130 --> 00:10:58.340
What would you like?

00:10:58.340 --> 00:11:00.260
Anything’s fine.

00:11:00.260 --> 00:11:01.680
Aside from eggs, that is.

00:11:01.680 --> 00:11:03.220
Are you a moron?

00:11:03.220 --> 00:11:05.940
The chances of landing on eggs is two in one hundred.

00:11:05.940 --> 00:11:07.180
You can’t get it, even if you aimed for it.

00:11:08.070 --> 00:11:12.320
I’m good with aiming lightly for either
salt or sugar, which have the greatest odds.

00:11:17.190 --> 00:11:19.400
All right, let’s get sugar or salt!

00:11:19.400 --> 00:11:21.910
Oh, amazing!

00:11:28.840 --> 00:11:31.130
You’re amazing, Kawachi!

00:11:31.130 --> 00:11:32.750
Move it!

00:11:32.750 --> 00:11:35.810
You’re really a completely useless man.

00:11:38.060 --> 00:11:40.340
But, there is no need to worry.

00:11:40.340 --> 00:11:44.230
Suwabara Kai, who has attained the
way of the sword, has now taken over.

00:11:46.010 --> 00:11:47.890
With this type of ball play,

00:11:47.890 --> 00:11:52.030
I’ll have no trouble landing the ball on any slot I desire.

00:11:54.990 --> 00:11:56.940
We’ll leave it to you, Suwa-chan!

00:11:57.510 --> 00:11:58.700
Just watch.

00:11:58.700 --> 00:12:01.410
Azuma got eggs in slot #78,

00:12:01.410 --> 00:12:03.450
and Baldy got eggs in slot #80.

00:12:03.450 --> 00:12:07.450
I’ll aim for sugar in the slot #79 between them!

00:12:13.220 --> 00:12:13.960
Amazing!

00:12:19.050 --> 00:12:20.590
Now, just watch.

00:12:20.590 --> 00:12:22.470
Suwabara style’s ultimate technique:

00:12:22.470 --> 00:12:25.020
Dragon at the Summit!

00:12:40.040 --> 00:12:40.860
He did it!

00:12:40.860 --> 00:12:41.730
It’s sugar!

00:12:44.240 --> 00:12:45.740
So close...

00:12:45.740 --> 00:12:47.080
You’re a moron!

00:12:47.080 --> 00:12:49.290
If you can aim with so much precision,

00:12:49.290 --> 00:12:53.330
why couldn’t you aim for it in that
area, where the sugars are all lined up?!

00:12:54.850 --> 00:12:56.800
I’m not like you.

00:12:56.800 --> 00:12:58.590
I won’t do cowardly things like that.

00:12:58.920 --> 00:13:01.090
H-He really is a moron...

00:13:01.540 --> 00:13:03.340
Amazing!

00:13:03.340 --> 00:13:06.510
I’ve never seen so many eggs before!

00:13:06.510 --> 00:13:06.730
Eggs! Eggs!

00:13:06.730 --> 00:13:09.350
H-He’s a moron, too...
Eggs! Eggs!

00:13:11.700 --> 00:13:14.520
What are you, a moron?!
It’s no time to be getting happy, is it?

00:13:14.520 --> 00:13:15.070
Huh?

00:13:15.520 --> 00:13:18.820
Oh top of things being hard
for Japan, with our loss in points,

00:13:18.820 --> 00:13:21.200
we have neither salt nor sugar.

00:13:21.200 --> 00:13:22.990
With only eggs and flour,

00:13:22.990 --> 00:13:25.070
any bread we make would be tasteless.

00:13:26.320 --> 00:13:30.200
But, didn’t he say that we can use any flour?

00:13:30.200 --> 00:13:32.500
And so, what about that?!

00:13:32.500 --> 00:13:34.150
I can’t take this anymore.

00:13:34.150 --> 00:13:35.920
In that case, it’s all right.

00:13:35.920 --> 00:13:38.050
What’s all right?

00:13:38.650 --> 00:13:40.540
It’ll be <i>Japan</i> #21!

00:13:42.640 --> 00:13:45.300
A bread that we can make with just these ingredients.

00:13:45.300 --> 00:13:47.300
With just these...?

00:13:47.690 --> 00:13:48.720
Yeah.

00:13:48.720 --> 00:13:50.800
That’s <i>Japan</i> #21.

00:14:04.660 --> 00:14:05.750
It’s no good.

00:14:05.750 --> 00:14:08.410
Even with Azuma’s <i>Japan</i>...

00:14:08.830 --> 00:14:11.200
This is the end!

00:14:11.200 --> 00:14:15.410
With only eggs and flour, any bread
we make would be completely tasteless.

00:14:15.410 --> 00:14:18.420
Like I said, that’s not true!

00:14:18.420 --> 00:14:21.210
They said that we can use any type of flour, after all.

00:14:21.210 --> 00:14:22.170
But...

00:14:22.170 --> 00:14:23.630
It’s all right.

00:14:23.630 --> 00:14:25.680
Let’s leave it to <i>Japan</i> #21.

00:14:30.400 --> 00:14:33.230
That looks like quite a grave turn of events.

00:14:33.230 --> 00:14:35.150
It’s not a laughing matter.

00:14:35.930 --> 00:14:40.090
We have already invested all of our savings in this.

00:14:40.090 --> 00:14:43.400
While this may have nothing
to do with paupers like you,

00:14:43.400 --> 00:14:47.070
if by some chance Azuma and they were to lose, I...

00:14:47.070 --> 00:14:50.490
Forget about preventing the takeover,
I’d lose even the management of this store.

00:14:50.490 --> 00:14:52.700
I’m thinking no such thing.

00:14:52.700 --> 00:14:55.660
I’m just worried about Azuma and everyone.

00:14:56.430 --> 00:15:00.420
Nothing will happen with us worrying unnecessarily.

00:15:00.420 --> 00:15:02.180
B-But...

00:15:02.180 --> 00:15:04.420
Well, if we lose,

00:15:04.420 --> 00:15:07.930
if we all seriously work at boring
jobs, little by little, it might work out.

00:15:08.390 --> 00:15:10.010
Exactly, Tsukino.

00:15:10.010 --> 00:15:13.140
As long as people can work
seriously, there’s nothing to fear.

00:15:13.820 --> 00:15:17.140
Even boring jobs, little by little...

00:15:17.140 --> 00:15:19.360
Here, let’s be safe and bet on 246.

00:15:19.360 --> 00:15:23.480
Exactly how much of what
you people say should I believe?

00:15:23.480 --> 00:15:24.900
There it is! Ron!

00:15:24.900 --> 00:15:26.400
Tsukino-san...

00:15:26.400 --> 00:15:29.750
I’m working at a boring job, seriously, little by little.

00:15:30.660 --> 00:15:32.170
Man...

00:15:34.670 --> 00:15:35.870
You’re cruel.

00:15:36.290 --> 00:15:40.510
But, jokes aside, this is quite a pinch they’re in...

00:15:40.510 --> 00:15:43.970
But Azuma-kun looks like he’s thought of something.

00:15:43.970 --> 00:15:45.880
We should just stay calm here.

00:15:48.140 --> 00:15:51.680
So, what’s this <i>Japan</i> #21?

00:15:51.680 --> 00:15:53.560
What kind of item is it?

00:15:53.560 --> 00:15:54.640
You see...

00:15:54.940 --> 00:15:56.730
Are they all right?

00:15:59.450 --> 00:16:02.310
What are you planning to do, Azuma?

00:16:02.770 --> 00:16:04.570
And that’s what it’ll turn out like.

00:16:04.570 --> 00:16:07.610
Can we really do something like that?

00:16:07.610 --> 00:16:11.160
No, it’s true that that might work out.

00:16:11.160 --> 00:16:13.620
Just as expected of the man who defeated me.

00:16:13.620 --> 00:16:15.830
A great difference in the ability to
conceptualize, compared to Baldy here.

00:16:15.830 --> 00:16:17.250
What was that?!

00:16:17.250 --> 00:16:20.540
Let’s ask if they have
something like that here, shall we?

00:16:20.540 --> 00:16:21.790
Yeah!

00:16:21.790 --> 00:16:25.680
Hey, Old Man Pierrot!

00:16:30.300 --> 00:16:32.090
Did you have a question?

00:16:32.630 --> 00:16:34.550
Old Man Pierrot, actually...

00:16:34.550 --> 00:16:36.550
What is he doing?

00:16:36.550 --> 00:16:39.600
I want that kind of flour, so...

00:16:40.700 --> 00:16:41.850
Well?

00:16:41.850 --> 00:16:44.190
I can get you that flour.

00:16:44.190 --> 00:16:44.820
Is that so?

00:16:46.080 --> 00:16:47.070
However...

00:16:47.410 --> 00:16:50.030
I am only 22 years old.

00:16:50.030 --> 00:16:51.910
I am not an old man!

00:16:51.910 --> 00:16:54.280
Should you call me an old man again...

00:16:55.250 --> 00:16:57.120
I shall hang you there!

00:16:57.120 --> 00:16:59.340
The trapeze swing?!

00:17:00.550 --> 00:17:03.370
Last year, I hung around two people there, also.

00:17:04.260 --> 00:17:09.100
Apparently, they dried out like
the “dry fish” you find in Japan.

00:17:10.680 --> 00:17:13.380
This year, you may be the victim.

00:17:16.150 --> 00:17:17.810
Be careful, Azuma.

00:17:17.810 --> 00:17:19.770
This man’s serious!

00:17:19.770 --> 00:17:20.520
That’s right,

00:17:20.520 --> 00:17:22.780
this is “serious,” on the world level!

00:17:23.490 --> 00:17:28.440
Oh, don’t get mad, Old... I mean,
really handsome Mister Pierrot.

00:17:28.440 --> 00:17:29.400
I was kidding.

00:17:30.620 --> 00:17:32.790
As long as you understand...

00:17:37.630 --> 00:17:40.620
All right, every type of flour is available here.

00:17:40.620 --> 00:17:42.330
You can take whatever you like.

00:17:43.050 --> 00:17:45.040
Just as you’d expect of the world level.

00:17:45.040 --> 00:17:45.900
Thank you.

00:17:47.430 --> 00:17:48.920
Oh, this is it.

00:17:49.550 --> 00:17:52.590
I cannot forgive the fact
that he insulted me,

00:17:52.590 --> 00:17:53.920
but this young boy...

00:17:54.490 --> 00:17:58.060
He has noticed what nobody did last year.

00:17:58.940 --> 00:18:00.350
That was scary, wasn’t it?

00:18:00.350 --> 00:18:02.100
That Old... Brother Pierrot...

00:18:02.660 --> 00:18:04.230
It’s true that he’s very agile,

00:18:04.230 --> 00:18:06.610
but that clown is no ordinary person.

00:18:06.610 --> 00:18:07.940
Yeah...

00:18:07.940 --> 00:18:09.900
Those malicious little eyes...

00:18:09.900 --> 00:18:10.810
I’m sure he’s a pervert.

00:18:12.110 --> 00:18:13.860
Kawachi, Suwabara,

00:18:13.860 --> 00:18:15.570
let’s make <i>Japan</i> #21.

00:18:15.570 --> 00:18:17.450
Yeah, let’s hurry up.

00:18:17.450 --> 00:18:20.580
There seem to be countries
that are already baking their bread.

00:18:21.670 --> 00:18:23.580
This platform has an oven attached.

00:18:24.070 --> 00:18:26.800
It seems like they have decided
on what bread they will be making.

00:18:27.430 --> 00:18:31.300
The question is how they’ll make up for
the handicap of not having salt or sugar.

00:18:31.300 --> 00:18:32.090
No...

00:18:32.090 --> 00:18:33.130
How they’ll overcome it.

00:18:33.130 --> 00:18:35.090
Good luck, everyone.

00:18:49.990 --> 00:18:51.110
I see!

00:18:53.160 --> 00:18:55.110
That is all!

00:18:57.600 --> 00:19:00.620
It’s good that we somehow managed to finish it,

00:19:00.620 --> 00:19:04.410
but we really made bread without any sugar or salt...

00:19:04.410 --> 00:19:06.330
Is it really all right like this?

00:19:06.330 --> 00:19:08.080
All right then, everyone...

00:19:08.080 --> 00:19:09.710
Since you are all done,

00:19:09.710 --> 00:19:11.880
the judging of the first preliminaries will begin.

00:19:11.880 --> 00:19:14.140
The judge shall be me, Pierrot.

00:19:15.430 --> 00:19:18.220
It looks like it’s about to finally start.

00:19:18.220 --> 00:19:21.430
But, how in the world is he going to judge?

00:19:21.430 --> 00:19:23.600
Won’t he just eat them?

00:19:23.600 --> 00:19:28.020
In the finals, where there’s only
a few countries, that’s possible.

00:19:28.020 --> 00:19:31.610
However, in the preliminaries, there are 135 countries!

00:19:31.610 --> 00:19:34.780
It’s not possible to taste all of them by himself.

00:19:34.780 --> 00:19:36.780
Yeah, not even he could...

00:19:36.780 --> 00:19:37.700
I know!

00:19:37.700 --> 00:19:41.370
Just like Old Man Kuroyanagi, I’m
sure that he can judge simply by looking.

00:19:42.840 --> 00:19:46.410
It’s true that he probably has that level of insight,

00:19:46.410 --> 00:19:50.370
but while this may consist entirely of young
people, they’re all bakers at the world level.

00:19:51.600 --> 00:19:55.010
It can’t all just be bread that you
can judge by simply looking at it.

00:19:56.640 --> 00:19:58.680
So, how is he...?

00:19:59.640 --> 00:20:01.380
You, Baldy over there!

00:20:01.380 --> 00:20:03.350
That is quite a valid question.

00:20:03.810 --> 00:20:04.970
All right.

00:20:04.970 --> 00:20:07.390
So, let me show you how I will be judging.

00:20:25.160 --> 00:20:27.660
W-What’s this smoke?!

00:20:27.660 --> 00:20:28.750
Don’t panic!

00:20:28.750 --> 00:20:30.110
It’s just some trick to frighten us.

00:20:30.110 --> 00:20:31.170
It’s scary!

00:20:34.470 --> 00:20:36.510
The Pierrots just keep multiplying!

00:20:36.510 --> 00:20:39.630
My last count was about 135!

00:20:39.630 --> 00:20:41.680
It’s like a festival!

00:20:41.980 --> 00:20:44.560
Artisans, were you surprised?

00:20:44.560 --> 00:20:47.310
My magic is at the world level as well.

00:20:47.310 --> 00:20:50.180
Increasing my numbers to 135
is a piece of cake for me.

00:20:50.180 --> 00:20:53.440
The fearsome world level!

00:20:53.440 --> 00:20:55.940
All right then, judging begins!

00:20:58.030 --> 00:20:59.940
Moving quickly, moving quickly!

00:20:59.940 --> 00:21:02.160
No! No! No!

00:21:02.800 --> 00:21:05.620
Chile, Mongolia, and Russia’s breads get 0 points.

00:21:05.620 --> 00:21:06.870
How can you say that?

00:21:06.870 --> 00:21:08.870
How can you give 0 points without tasting it?!

00:21:08.870 --> 00:21:10.870
Because I am a clown!

00:21:11.170 --> 00:21:12.870
Perestroika!!

00:21:13.800 --> 00:21:16.250
Once you’re a world level clown,

00:21:16.250 --> 00:21:18.210
you can even discern from an audience of 10,000

00:21:18.210 --> 00:21:22.840
as to exactly which person will laugh, and where.

00:21:22.840 --> 00:21:27.430
All of you who did not get sugar or salt in the roulette

00:21:27.430 --> 00:21:31.890
have made your bread without
any trick to it, just as you were told.

00:21:31.890 --> 00:21:33.600
I can see that in one glance.

00:21:37.080 --> 00:21:38.780
Just like Japan,

00:21:38.780 --> 00:21:41.610
Russia also didn’t get sugar or salt, eh?

00:21:42.200 --> 00:21:45.240
With them, they get off with 0 points.

00:21:45.240 --> 00:21:47.490
If we get 0 points,

00:21:47.490 --> 00:21:51.120
we’ll have to go to the
second preliminaries with -2 points!

00:21:51.120 --> 00:21:53.880
Man, whose fault is this?!

00:21:56.130 --> 00:21:59.220
Azuma-kun, are we really all right?!

00:22:04.020 --> 00:22:05.770
It’s finally going to start.

00:22:06.690 --> 00:22:09.600
It’s true that the bread they made is different,

00:22:09.600 --> 00:22:12.600
but just like the Russian team,
the Japanese team

00:22:12.600 --> 00:22:15.400
hasn’t used any sugar or salt...

00:22:15.400 --> 00:22:17.190
Is it really all right?

00:22:20.690 --> 00:22:22.650
Japanese representatives.

00:22:22.650 --> 00:22:24.700
I will begin the scoring...

00:22:25.340 --> 00:22:28.910
of this bread, which has neither salt nor sugar in it.

00:24:05.520 --> 00:24:07.430
Bread with neither sugar nor salt...

00:24:07.430 --> 00:24:09.140
Will it really be all right?

00:24:09.140 --> 00:24:10.600
Don’t get flustered, Kawachi!

00:24:10.600 --> 00:24:11.940
The judging is beginning!

00:24:11.940 --> 00:24:13.400
Zunchan zunchan zunchan zunchan

00:24:13.400 --> 00:24:16.150
Pierrot No. 1, Telephone No. 2.

00:24:16.150 --> 00:24:17.470
Snacks at 3 p.m.!!

00:24:17.470 --> 00:24:19.150
It’s <i>Japan</i> #21.

00:24:19.150 --> 00:24:19.890
Be sure to watch!

00:24:20.450 --> 00:24:22.640
Yakitate!! Seed of knowledge.

00:24:22.640 --> 00:24:23.710
The Japanese people are ranked highly in
the world when it comes to liking eggs.

00:24:23.710 --> 00:24:26.020
<i>Ranked highly in the world
The Japanese people are ranked highly in
the world when it comes to liking eggs.</i>

00:24:26.020 --> 00:24:29.290
The consumption of eggs in a
year is over 300 per capita.

00:24:29.290 --> 00:24:31.130
That means they eat at least one egg a day.

00:24:31.130 --> 00:24:31.660
Isn’t that amazing?

00:24:31.660 --> 00:24:33.840
Really?!
